  "body": "Found while fixing #2719 (PR #2732).\n\nWhat happens: when the curved-face fit cannot measure a face, the import reports the face `UNMEASURED` and the model is reduced fidelity. Verify then refuses each operation with `model_fidelity::TOO_COARSE`: \"imported too coarsely to verify; re-import with a larger STEP facet budget\". A larger facet budget does not help this face. Only the warn log line names the true cause (`step: face <n> keeps the kernel's facets unmeasured (<reason>)`).\n\nExpected: the refusal names the cause, for example \"a curved face of the model could not be measured\", and does not advise a larger budget.\n\nOption: measure the kept kernel mesh of that face with a nearest-point search (see `docs/decisions/2719-step-fit-fallback-diagnostic.md`). Then a fine kernel mesh stays at full fidelity.\n\nDone means: the user-facing refusal for an unmeasured face names that cause, and a test pins the text.\n",
